@startuml Electron Audit Verification Flow
title Native Electron Audit Receipt and Restore Check

actor User
participant "Electron main\nmain.js" as Main
participant "Local receipt\naudit-anchor.js" as Anchor
participant "macOS Keychain\naudit-keychain helper" as Keychain
participant "Native backend\nprivate audit route" as Route
participant "Audit verifier\nauditVerificationService.js" as Verifier
participant "Retention planner\nauditRetentionService.js" as Retention
database "PostgreSQL\naudit chain + domain rows" as DB

Main -> Anchor: Read HMAC-signed receipt and safeStorage key
Anchor -> Keychain: Read latest checkpoint digest
Keychain --> Anchor: Matching witness or unavailable
Anchor --> Main: Trusted checkpoint or uninitialized
Main -> Route: POST /verify (loopback + per-launch token; checkpoint if present)
Route -> Verifier: verifyAuditHistory(trustedCheckpoint)
Verifier -> DB: Scan chain, domain links, schema heads, cutover
DB --> Verifier: Current rows and head
Verifier --> Route: verified | partially_verified | unavailable | failed
Route --> Main: ADR-026 envelope with status

alt new cluster this launch, no receipt, fully checked head, zero legacy counts
  Main -> Anchor: Sign first checkpoint at current post-migration head
  Anchor -> Keychain: Create independent checkpoint record
  Main -> Route: POST /checkpoint metadata
  Main -> Main: Enable trusted live session
else exact verified startup head
  Main -> Main: Enable trusted live session
else partial at startup or no trusted receipt
  Main -> Main: Notify; do not promote existing tail
end

opt existing installation has no trusted receipt and user chooses enrollment
  User -> Main: Start audit protection
  Main -> Verifier: Recheck complete current chain without receipt
  Verifier --> Main: Internally valid head and legacy cutover
  Main --> User: Default-Cancel warning; earlier authenticity cannot be proved
  User -> Main: Confirm
  Main -> Anchor: Sign head with immutable enrollment sequence
  Anchor -> Keychain: Create independent checkpoint witness
  Main -> Route: POST /checkpoint metadata
  Main -> Main: Enable forward-looking live closure
end

User -> Main: Open Admin audit view or export snapshot
Main -> Anchor: Read authenticated local receipt
Anchor -> Keychain: Compare checkpoint record
Main -> Route: POST /read (checkpoint, cursor, page limit)
Route -> Verifier: Verify complete chain in read-only snapshot
Verifier -> DB: Scan chain and linked domain rows
Route -> DB: Read page from the same snapshot
Route --> Main: Verification, anchored/pending entries, hasMore
alt verified page
  Main --> User: Label enrollment baseline; show page or save complete snapshot (max 500 entries, 2 MB)
else failed or unavailable
  Main --> User: Show status without entries or export
end

opt trusted live session enabled
  loop every 30 seconds while backend healthy
    Main -> Route: Re-verify full chain and cutover
    Route --> Main: Valid new tail or failure
    alt valid new tail
      Main -> Anchor: Persist signed new checkpoint
      Anchor -> Keychain: Replace latest checkpoint record
      Main -> Route: POST /checkpoint metadata
      Route -> DB: Insert metadata for existing local receipt
    else failed or unavailable
      Main -> Main: End session and notify
    end
  end
end

opt trusted live session; daily retention attempt
  Main -> Route: POST /retention-plan with authenticated checkpoint
  Route -> Retention: Verify full history and find complete year-old prefix
  Retention -> DB: Read eligible boundary and linked high-water IDs
  Retention --> Main: Sequence, hash, domain IDs, migration heads
  Main -> Anchor: Sign retention boundary before deletion
  Anchor -> Keychain: Replace checkpoint witness
  Main -> Route: POST /checkpoint metadata; POST /retention-prune
  Route -> Retention: Verify signed boundary and retained chain
  Retention -> DB: Guarded atomic prefix prune under head lock
  DB --> Main: Deleted count or exact retry (zero)
end

User -> Main: Request native update
Main -> Route: POST /update-decision (checksum or install decision)
Route -> DB: Append release_update chain event
Route --> Main: Sequence and hash
alt receipt exists or a trusted session was established
  Main -> Anchor: Close verified checkpoint synchronously
  Main -> Main: Block install if closure fails
else no receipt and no trusted session
  Main -> Main: Report unavailable; update may continue
end
note right of Main
  This records Electron's local decision.
  It does not prove publisher signature or release provenance.
end note

User -> Main: Request native backup restore
Main -> Main: Pause live closure; stage database and attachments
Main -> Route: Verify candidate against unchanged local receipt
Route --> Main: Verification status
alt status is verified
  Main -> Main: Finalize database switch
else any other status
  Main -> Main: Roll back candidate database and attachments
  alt rollback succeeds and user accepts second warning
    Main -> Route: Verify selected backup's full internal chain without receipt
    Route --> Main: Internally valid or failed
    alt internally valid
      Main -> Main: Finalize one retry; keep old receipt; continuity unverified
    else invalid
      Main -> Main: Roll back retry
    end
  else cancel or rollback failure
    Main -> Main: Keep original database; do not retry
  end
end

note over Anchor,DB
  The Keychain checkpoint is outside PostgreSQL and app data.
  Missing or mismatched sides fail closed; no silent re-enrollment.
end note

@enduml
